def read_user_profile(user_id, replica):
    if replica.is_partitioned_from_primary():
        if ALLOW_STALE_READS:
            return replica.read(user_id)     # AP: serve what we have
        raise ServiceUnavailable("cannot guarantee consistency during partition")  # CP: refuse
    return replica.read(user_id)
```

This is the whole theorem in eight lines: the partition check is the fork, and `ALLOW_STALE_READS` is the product decision an interviewer wants you to name explicitly, not just imply.
